WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.540
Computers first took up
an entire room.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:04.920
Then they fit on your
desk.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.760
Then the next thing you
knew, they were portable

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.250
folding devices that
could sit on your lap.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.880
Since then, laptops have
become even smaller and

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.030
more lightweight, yet
more and more powerful.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.400
With its lightning fast
processor and dazzling

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.310
graphics. This laptop is
designed for high

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.510
performance gaming.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.150
And if that's not cool
enough, you can light up

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:33.150
the keyboard in a choice
of nearly 17 million

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.400
colors. The computer's
brain.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.490
The motherboard begins
as a printed circuit

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:41.670
board. Its pattern of
lines and pads and copper

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:44.040
is the wiring for the
electronic components

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.900
that will be soldered to
the board.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.720
This machine places a
stencil of the component

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.540
layout onto the board
and applies solder paste

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:52.860
through the openings.

